---
import Doc from "../layouts/Doc.astro";

/*
 * Etap 1.12, before registration opens: the controller is named here only as
 * akApp Studio. Under an unregistered business (NDG) the controller is a
 * natural person, so add the full name and address to "Who is responsible",
 * and the same in terms.astro.
 */
const TOC = [
  { id: "responsible", label: "Who is responsible" },
  { id: "collect", label: "What we collect" },
  { id: "basis", label: "Why, and on what legal basis" },
  { id: "device", label: "What is stored on your device" },
  { id: "processors", label: "Who processes your data for us" },
  { id: "retention", label: "How long we keep it" },
  { id: "rights", label: "Your rights" },
  { id: "children", label: "Children" },
  { id: "security", label: "Security" },
  { id: "changes", label: "Changes to this policy" },
];
---
<Doc
  title="Privacy Policy · Xebeka"
  description="What personal data Xebeka collects, why, who helps process it, and what rights you have."
  heading="Privacy Policy"
  updated="27 September 2026"
  toc={TOC}
>
  <p>
    This policy explains what personal data Xebeka collects, why, who helps us process it, and what
    rights you have. We collect only what the game needs. There are no ads, no tracking and no
    analytics, and we never sell data.
  </p>

  <h2 id="responsible">Who is responsible</h2>
  <p>
    The controller of your data is <a href="https://akappstudio.pl">akApp Studio</a>. For anything
    about your data, write to <a href="mailto:kontakt@xebeka.com">kontakt@xebeka.com</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="collect">What we collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Your account:</strong> your email address and your password. The password is stored
      only in hashed form, so nobody can read it, us included. If you sign in with Google, we receive
      from Google only your email address and the ID Google uses for your account, instead of a
      password.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Your characters:</strong> their names, sex, world and progress in the game, with the
      dates they were created and last saved.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Technical data:</strong> when you use the site or the game, our providers record your
      IP address, your browser and the requests it makes, to keep the service secure and to fix
      problems.
    </li>
    <li><strong>Messages:</strong> whatever you write to us by email.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>You do not have to give us your email address, but without it we cannot create an account for you.</p>

  <h2 id="basis">Why, and on what legal basis</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      To create and run your account and characters, and to send the emails that come with them:
      confirming your address, resetting your password, and important notices about your account or
      the game. This is needed to provide the game you signed up for (Article 6(1)(b) GDPR).
    </li>
    <li>
      To keep the game secure, prevent abuse and enforce the rules of play. This is our legitimate
      interest in a safe and fair game (Article 6(1)(f) GDPR).
    </li>
    <li>To answer your messages. This is our legitimate interest in replying (Article 6(1)(f) GDPR).</li>
    <li>To keep or hand over data when the law requires it (Article 6(1)(c) GDPR).</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We do not send newsletters or marketing email.</p>

  <h2 id="device">What is stored on your device</h2>
  <p>
    The site and the game keep a few things in your browser's local storage: your sign-in session,
    your game settings and window layout, and the game data the game needs while you play. The game
    cannot work without them, so we do not ask for consent. The forms for creating an account, logging
    in and resetting a password also run Cloudflare's bot check, which uses only what it needs to
    tell people from bots. There are no advertising or tracking cookies.
  </p>

  <h2 id="processors">Who processes your data for us</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Supabase</strong> stores accounts and characters and handles signing in. Our database
      is in Frankfurt, Germany.
    </li>
    <li><strong>Vercel</strong> hosts the website and the game.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>Cloudflare</strong> checks that the forms for creating an account, logging in and
      resetting a password are used by people, not bots. For this it looks at technical signals such
      as your IP address and browser. Cloudflare also uses these signals on its own account to
      improve the check, as its
      <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/turnstile-privacy-policy/">Turnstile privacy notice</a>
      explains.
    </li>
    <li><strong>SEOHOST</strong>, in Poland, handles our email.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>Google</strong>, only if you choose to sign in with Google. Your Google account itself
      is covered by Google's own privacy policy.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Apart from what Cloudflare does on its own account, they process data only on our instructions.
    Supabase, Vercel and Cloudflare are US companies, so some data
    may be processed outside the European Economic Area. Those transfers are protected by the EU-US
    Data Privacy Framework or by the European Commission's Standard Contractual Clauses.
  </p>

  <h2 id="retention">How long we keep it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Account and character data: until you delete your account.</li>
    <li>A character you delete: 7 days, the time you have to change your mind.</li>
    <li>Technical logs: for the short time our providers keep them, usually days to weeks.</li>
    <li>Emails: as long as it takes to deal with your matter.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="rights">Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    You can ask us for a copy of your data, to correct it, to delete it, to limit how we use it, or
    to send it to you in a portable format. You can also object to what we do on the basis of our
    legitimate interests. Write to <a href="mailto:kontakt@xebeka.com">kontakt@xebeka.com</a> and we
    will answer within one month. You can delete your account yourself at any time.
  </p>
  <p>
    You can complain to a data protection authority: in Poland, the President of the Personal Data
    Protection Office (<a href="https://uodo.gov.pl">uodo.gov.pl</a>), or the authority in the
    country where you live. If you live outside the European Union, for example in Brazil, you have
    the rights your own law gives you, and we honour them the same way.
  </p>

  <h2 id="children">Children</h2>
  <p>
    Xebeka is for players aged 13 and over. If we learn that an account belongs to a child under 13,
    we delete it. A parent who thinks their child has made an account can write to us.
  </p>

  <h2 id="security">Security</h2>
  <p>
    Connections to the site and the game are encrypted, passwords are stored only in hashed form,
    and each player can reach only their own account and characters.
  </p>

  <h2 id="changes">Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    When this policy changes, the new version appears here with a new date, and significant changes
    are announced on the site.
  </p>
</Doc>
